From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a display says which connector it is on

The compositor names a monitor with no EDID make, model or serial after
its connector ("HDMI-A-1"), as sway does. Only the GPU process reads the
connector, so:

- CreateDisplaySnapshot sets DisplaySnapshot::domicile_connector from
  the connector's type and number (domicile/connector_name.cc).
- DisplaySnapshot's mojom carries it to the browser process, and Clone()
  keeps it.
- OzonePlatform::GetDomicileConnectors lends DrmScreen's connectors to
  the browser, since display::Display has no field for them. Every other
  platform has none.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
